Well, this was an unexpected ascension.
I ascended a valkyrie fairly recently and decided to try a different 
character.I read about a bit and started a rogue, expecting to die a 
great many times before finally ascending or giving up on rogues.
Instead, this is the very first rogue I have ever played with and its an 
ascension!
The early game had a blessed +3 shield of reflection in a shop, a BoH 
somewhere in the gnomish mines, as well as a deadly bones file at minetown.
A previous character had left behind 10 named baby silver dragons, as 
well as 2 BoHs, many potions/scrolls, a [oMR, +2 speed boots,+2 SDSM and 
some minor trinkets.
I managed to kill the baby silver dragons via liberal usage of the 
E-word and a _lot_ of dagger throwing.
Shortly after IDing all of the loot, making of much holy water I managed 
to blow up both uncursed BoHs and all of my potions, food, scrolls, 
wands, etc etc.All I had left was a cursed BoH.
I persevered undaunted and managed to recover from this blunder as I 
still had MR, reflection, speed and 41 daggers at expert skill.

I picked p a lamp on the next level, rubbed it and got a wish!
There was nothing I particularly needed so I got a "oLifeSaving. (this 
was a good choice as it turns out...)

I got Teleport control off of the first tengu I killed, but had to eat 
about 30 leprechauns before I finally got teleportitis!
Normally it's the other way around...

I did the dishwasher dance until I was eligible for the quest and then 
did the Rogue quest with aid of my daggers and some cursed scrolls of 
teleportation.
I am compelled to mention the crappy quest artifact and almost useless 
Rogue Deity, an eternal curse upon both of them! (especially you, Kos!)

At some point around here I decided to not genocide anything, instead I 
used any genocide scrolls I found for nurse-dancing at sokoban.

I used a silver dragon at medusa to create a bridge across to Medusa as 
I had no means of levitation yet.While I was dancing with the dragon on 
the frozen moat a red Naga spawned right around the corner from me, 
breathed fire at me and I drowned!
Luckily my "oLifeSaving saved me and put me on a dry island in the 
middle of nowhere!
The silver dragon created a bridge to me and then stood on it, blocking 
my movement.I whipped out my wand of teleport only to discover it was dry!
I was wearing my "oMagicBreathing so I was safe from the red naga now, 
but I didnt want to kill the silver dragon, so I stood there trying to 
wrest out the final charge to keep the silver dragon 'safe'.
Luckily it worked and I killed the red naga safely and bridged the moat 
with ice.
Medusa was the usual pushover. (apply blindfold, enter room, whoops, 
where did medusa go?, where did that statue come from?)
Perseus' statue yielded nothing, very disappointing.

The castle itself was pretty simple, I used the drawbridge to kill 
almost everyone until some spoilsport destroyed it with a wand of striking.
I think I used the castle wand for magic markers and gauntlets of dexterity.
Here I decided to dual-wield 2 silver sabers for the rest of the game, 
in addition to my (now) 41 +7 rustproof daggers (21 of which were kept 
in the BoH).No better weapons had popped up and I really didnt feel like 
altar camping.I blessed my silver sabers, enchanted them to +7 and 
practiced until the skill maxed out, then I went dual +7 Silver sabers 
for the rest of the game.
At some point I decided to genocide disenchanters as they were really 
annoying me and I was all out of scrolls of EA and EW! (oddly enough the 
arch-liches weren't annoying at all)
The rest was pretty unexceptional until I got my brains eaten twice 
while invading rodneys sanctum!
I was very annoyed at the time, but I had almost everything essential on 
me, which I just #name'd. Gehennom had paths dug between the stairs so 
magic mapping wasnt needed there. Luckily I didnt forget which scroll 
was identify, so I was able to ID almost everything when I got back to 
my stash.
The final run was pretty unexceptional except in being very quick.
When I got to astral i put on a blindfold and used to telepathy to see 
which corner had the most aligned priest and angels.I went there 
(killing pestilence once) and it was indeed my altar!
The "oY was offered and the rest is history...

